1. COLOR SYSTEM (DARK ORANGE DONE CORRECTLY)

Base Neutrals

Black Absolute     #0A0A0A   (main background)
Black Soft         #121212   (cards)
Black Lifted       #1A1A1A   (modals)
White Soft         #EDEDED   (primary text)
White Muted        #9A9A9A   (secondary text)

Accent (USE SPARINGLY)

Dark Orange        #F97316   (only for meaning)
Orange Glow        rgba(249,115,22,0.22)
Orange Mist        rgba(249,115,22,0.08)

🚫 Never use orange for:
	•	Paragraph text
	•	Icons by default
	•	Decorative backgrounds

Orange = intent, pulse, decision

⸻

2. GLASS SYSTEM (THIS IS WHAT YOU’RE MISSING)

This is the real secret.

Glass Card Token

background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04);
backdrop-filter: blur(16px);
border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);

Optional glow (only on focus):

box-shadow: 0 0 40px rgba(249,115,22,0.12);

Rules
	•	Glass is NEVER pure white
	•	Blur is always subtle
	•	Borders are almost invisible
	•	Glass only appears above darkness

Glass = depth, not decoration.

⸻

3. IMAGE SYSTEM (THIS IS THE BIG ONE)

Image Characteristics

Your images must be:
	•	Low contrast
	•	Slightly desaturated
	•	Soft focus or motion blur
	•	Grainy (film grain, not noise)
	•	Never sharp + never loud

Think:

dream, memory, reflection

Image Placement Rules
	•	Images are background layers, never foreground content
	•	Always partially obscured by:
	•	gradient
	•	glass
	•	darkness
	•	Never full brightness

Mandatory Overlay Stack

Every image gets this stack (top → bottom):

Text / UI
↓
Glass layer (blur)
↓
Dark gradient (black → transparent)
↓
Image

This creates the “looking through glass” effect.

⸻

4. GRADIENT SYSTEM (VERY CONTROLLED)

Allowed gradients only:

Ambient Gradient

Black → Transparent
Angle: vertical
Opacity: 60% → 0%

Accent Bloom (Rare)

Radial
Color: Dark Orange
Opacity: 8–12%
Blur: High

🚫 No rainbow gradients
🚫 No sharp transitions
🚫 No gradients inside buttons

Gradients simulate light leakage, not style.

⸻

5. GLOW SYSTEM (DO NOT OVERUSE)

Glow is status, not decoration.

Glow Rules
	•	Only one glow visible per screen
	•	Glow never touches edges
	•	Glow always blurred (40–80px)

Glow Types
	•	Orange glow → action / pulse / call
	•	White glow → focus / reading

If glow feels obvious → remove it.

⸻

6. TYPOGRAPHY SYSTEM (EDITORIAL, CALM)

Headlines
	•	Serif (Canela / Cormorant / Playfair)
	•	Weight: Regular or Medium
	•	Tracking: slightly tight
	•	Line-height: loose

Feels like a book sentence.

Body
	•	Sans (Inter / SF Pro)
	•	Small size
	•	Muted white
	•	Calm spacing

🚫 No bold paragraphs
🚫 No shouting

Text should feel confident enough to whisper.

⸻

7. MOTION SYSTEM (THIS SELLS PREMIUM)

Allowed:
	•	Slow fades (300–600ms)
	•	Breathing opacity (subtle loop)
	•	Vertical drift (2–6px)

Forbidden:
	•	Bounce
	•	Elastic
	•	Springy

Motion should feel like air moving, not UI reacting.

⸻

8. BUTTON SYSTEM (MINIMAL POWER)

Primary Button
	•	Background: White
	•	Text: Black
	•	Radius: Medium (not pill)
	•	On press: orange glow appears

Secondary
	•	Text-only
	•	Muted white → orange on hover

Buttons never compete visually.
They wait patiently.

⸻

9. GRAIN & TEXTURE (FINAL TOUCH)

This is why it feels “real”.
	•	Add subtle film grain overlay to:
	•	images
	•	backgrounds
	•	Opacity: 3–6%
	•	Static grain, not animated

This removes the “digital flatness”.

